 {"id":"RELEASE-2026-09-23-01","title":"[P1 BLOCKER] DF-BOARDCTL-8: Burndown renders 2 of 20 points — template passes window[start,end] as x-axis instead of per-day labels, discarding 18/20 data points","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"finding","created_at":"2026-09-23T04:48:00Z","created_by":"releng-sat","reasoning":"Measured on v0.1.7 release binary (sha256-verified). Payload derived.burndown = {window:[2026-09-03,2026-09-22] (2 bounds), open:[20 values]}. template.go:714 passes d.burndown.window as the days array to chartLines. chartLines derives xs from series[0].days (2 entries), so linePath draws only the 2 endpoints. Burndown silently discards 18/20 points and looks like a plausible down-trend rather than an obvious error. Burnup renders correctly (has a real per-day days array). Fix: add BurndownSeries.days (per-day labels, mirror BurnupSeries.days in derive.go:41) and pass it at template.go:714 + overlay site. Gate: payload-shape test asserting burndown.days.length === burndown.open.length. Evidence: DF-BOARDCTL-8 fingerprint 95c5312a. CI on f17253b (v0.1.7 tag): Multi-Arch 35551898349 + CI 35551880624 both success.","detail":{"fingerprint":"95c5312ada5106c989bdc6061ad8e810ce628b1c5570557d28cffe3916f5a81c"}}
 {"id":"RELEASE-2026-09-23-02","title":"[P1 BLOCKER] DF-BOARDCTL-9: One spec-invalid JSONL line kills ALL reads — 9 live fleet boards unreadable (helios 2347 rows, consensus 1338, ring-runner 33); validate offers no repair path","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"finding","created_at":"2026-09-23T04:48:00Z","created_by":"releng-sat","reasoning":"Dogfood run 2026-09-22: 53 boards scanned; 27 exit 1; 9 carry spec-invalid lines (raw newlines, truncated rows, bunker banner pasted mid-row). Any single bad line aborts the entire read: consensus 1338 bad lines, first at line 157 — 164 valid rows unreachable. Legacy pretty-printed-generation boards are the affected class. Fix two-part: (1) --skip-bad-lines degrade-with-evidence mode (report per-line parse errors, summarize REST, exit 1); (2) validate --repair that re-serializes salvageable rows via json-repair into tasks.rewritten.jsonl for operator review. Evidence: DF-BOARDCTL-9 fingerprint be4139a4. CI on f17253b: green (35551898349 + 35551880624).","detail":{"fingerprint":"be4139a4be9ca22ed1776a715e69f17bb607641c2cf1a9c0dceb1051b0fa2d11"}}
 {"id":"RELEASE-2026-09-23-03","title":"[P1 BLOCKER] REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001: Fleet-wide 352 rows carry off-vocabulary statuses (227 duplicate, 56 parked, 23 done, 16 open, 12 closed, 8 completed, 3 todo, 1 retired, 1 resolved) across ~28 boards","status":"pending","priority":"P1","type":"finding","created_at":"2026-09-23T04:48:00Z","created_by":"releng-sat","reasoning":"Fleet project review #15 scan: status=duplicate 227, parked 56, done 23, open 16, closed 12, completed 8, todo 3, retired 1, resolved 1 across ~28 boards. Root cause: dedup/cleanup pass wrote duplicate as a STATUS instead of a canonical status + marker field. Impact: validator errors on several boards; any consumer counting open work by status either counts 227 as open forever or drops them. boardctl validate already names the fix (boardctl update <ID> --status ...). Required: writer-side rule (reject/flag off-vocabulary values at write time, or boardctl dup <ID> --of <ID> writes a marker field) plus one fleet sweep. Blocking release because this is data-corruption-adjacent fleet-wide and the P1 was never resolved. Evidence: row id REVIEW-BOARDCTL-001 on this board.","detail":{}}
